cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use trainnr, please cite the software; if you build on its
  results, please cite the paper under preferred-citation.
type: software
title: "trainnr: the end-to-end robotics platform, a self-improvement flywheel for robots"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end robotics platform run from a coding agent: the robot's
  own telemetry becomes a content-hashed simulation model (real-to-sim),
  training datasets are generated with recorded provenance, policies are
  trained on the identified model with measured randomization spans,
  evaluated with paired trials and exact intervals, gated against the
  deployment runtime (sim-to-real), deployed, and watched through their
  telemetry for drift, which starts the next turn. One MCP server, a
  desktop app and a Claude Code plugin.
